{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:1", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Three cities, three paths, the all-ruling one: here the imperishable syllables are set; presiding over them is the unaging, ancient one, the greatest glory of the gods.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:tripura-triads"], "terms": ["trm:tripura"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:1-11", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1-11"}, "paraphrase": "Tripurā pervades three cities (worlds, bodies, states); her cakra has nine triangles (yoni) with their yoginīs; the fifteen nityās; the verse 'desire, womb, kalā…' encodes her fifteen-syllable mantra.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "ultimate"], "practices": ["prc:sricakra-bhavana"], "concepts": ["cpt:devi-as-brahman"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:10", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "10"}, "paraphrase": "The great lunar day, the fifteen Nityās, together with the sixteenth, bears the centre of the city.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:fifteen-nityas", "cpt:nityas-as-time"], "notes": "Obscure verse; paraphrase of the second half only.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:12-summary", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "12 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "A verse on Kaula offerings is recorded by summary only.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:13-16", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "13-16"}, "paraphrase": "Knowing her, one becomes the supreme; this is the knowledge of the Upaniṣad.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:14", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "14"}, "paraphrase": "Bhaga is Śakti and the blessed Kāma is the Lord; both here are givers of good fortune; they are equal in primacy, equal in being, equal in vigour; their Śakti is unaging, the womb of the universe.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:fivefold-equality", "cpt:siva-sakti-union"], "disputes": ["dsp:siva-sakti-primacy"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tripura-upanisad:2", "source": "src:tripura-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "They held nine yonis, nine cakras, nine yogas and nine yoginīs; the kindly lords of the nine cakras, nine mudrās, nine blessed ones of the earth.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:nine-avaranas", "cpt:ten-mudras-srividya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
